Web Traffic Analytics

Project Overview

Web Traffic Analytics examines website traffic data to understand user behavior, page performance, and visitor engagement.

Objectives

- Identify the most-viewed website pages.
- Analyze average session duration.
- Examine bounce rates and exit rates.
- Identify pages that may require improvement.
- Recommend strategies to improve user engagement.

Tools Used

- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib

Dataset

The project uses illustrative website traffic data containing page names, page views, session duration, bounce rate, and exit rate.

Methodology

1. Create and organize the dataset.
2. Calculate key website traffic metrics.
3. Group and compare performance across pages.
4. Visualize page views, session duration, and bounce rates.
5. Identify potential engagement issues.
6. Provide recommendations for website improvement.

Expected Outcomes

The analysis demonstrates how website traffic metrics can help identify popular pages and potential user engagement problems.

Conclusion

Web traffic analysis supports data-driven website improvements by highlighting page performance and areas that may require further investigation.

